00:45:57.443 --> 00:46:02.250
[JON GREEN] So for a cloud
code, it knows SQL very well.

00:46:02.790 --> 00:46:07.896
So what I would do is, you know,
create the schema in the spec.

00:46:08.340 --> 00:46:11.700
I would say, you know, we need,
you know, these fields or,

00:46:12.480 --> 00:46:15.411
you know, you could even go to a
higher level and say, you know,

00:46:15.444 --> 00:46:20.020
"I'm creating-- a database needs
to hold this data," and then

00:46:20.020 --> 00:46:23.997
have it create a schema, and
then just check to make sure

00:46:24.005 --> 00:46:26.620
that that schema makes sense.

00:46:27.120 --> 00:46:31.284
So you can either be very
specific and, you know,

00:46:31.290 --> 00:46:34.618
"This is exactly what I
want," or you can be more

00:46:34.653 --> 00:46:37.410
